-- title:
--   Left Tensor Pair Prefix Normalization
-- statement:
--   **Left-tensor outcome prefixes are normalized.** Let `A` and `B` be finite submeasurements and define `E_b = leftTensor (A.total * B.outcome b)`. Summing the positive products `E_b E_bᴴ` over the `B` outcomes gives an operator below the identity on the tensor product space.
--
--   $$
--   \sum_{b : β} E_b E_b^{\dagger} \le I_{ι \times ι}.
--   $$
--
--   This is the left-register normalization used by the reverse bounds in `evaluatedSlice_phaseSeven_second_reverse_bound` and `evaluatedSlice_phaseEight_tail_bound`.
--
--   Formalization credit: Sirui Lu, Ruixuan Deng, Yanqiao Zhu, and Zhengfeng Ji (arXiv:2609.19814). Mathematical source: Zhengfeng Ji, Anand Natarajan, Thomas Vidick, John Wright, and Henry Yuen (arXiv:2009.12982).
--
--   **Formalization Note.** The source declaration is `MIPStarRE.LDT.Commutativity.leftTensor_pair_prefix_normalization`; its Lean statement gives the exact quantifier order and all boundary hypotheses.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/LionSR/MIPStarRE/blob/f382c801026f53a9efc260fdee707cb35e0adb15/MIPStarRE/LDT/Commutativity/ScalarApproximation/PaperChainBasic/Normalization.lean#L393-L444

